From: =?UTF-8?q?Krzysztof=20Drobi=C5=84ski?= <krzysztof@kd-solutions.pl>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 17:12:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix passing GOFLAGS from Yocto environment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

OpenEmbedded's go-mod class adds -modcacherw to Go build flags so the
module cache remains writable and later clean/unpack tasks can remove it.

The Forgejo Makefile unconditionally assigns GOFLAGS, overriding recipe
exports. Make GOFLAGS overridable so distributions can provide required
Go flags through the build environment while preserving the default value
for normal upstream builds.

Upstream-Status: Pending [Yocto-specific build flags]

Signed-off-by: Krzysztof Drobiński <krzysztof@kd-solutions.pl>
---
 src/forgejo.org/Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/forgejo.org/Makefile b/forgejo.org/Makefile
index d1a1e90dec..de42b3c42a 100644
--- a/src/forgejo.org/Makefile
+++ b/src/forgejo.org/Makefile
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@ ifeq ($(HAS_GO), yes)
 	CGO_CFLAGS ?= $(shell $(GO) env CGO_CFLAGS) $(CGO_EXTRA_CFLAGS)
 endif
 
-GOFLAGS := -v
+GOFLAGS ?= -v
 EXECUTABLE ?= gitea
 
 ifeq ($(shell sed --version 2>/dev/null | grep -q GNU && echo gnu),gnu)
